## Struct Convex Client

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#91-95)

`pub struct ConvexClient { /* private fields */ }`

Expand description

An asynchronous client to interact with a specific project to perform mutations and manage query subscriptions using [`tokio`](https://docs.rs/tokio/1.50.0/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/tokio/index.html "mod tokio").

The Convex client requires a deployment url, which can be found in the [dashboard](https://dashboard.convex.dev/) settings tab.

```
use convex::ConvexClient;
use futures::StreamExt;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
    let mut sub = client.subscribe("listMessages", maplit::btreemap!{}).await?;
    while let Some(result) = sub.next().await {
        println!("{result:?}");
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

The [`ConvexClient`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html "struct convex::ConvexClient") internally holds a connection and a [`tokio`](https://docs.rs/tokio/1.50.0/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/tokio/index.html "mod tokio") background task to manage it. It is advised that you create one and **reuse** it. You can safely clone with [`ConvexClient::clone()`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#method.clone "method convex::ConvexClient::clone") to share the connection and outstanding subscriptions.

### [§](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#examples)Examples

For example code, please refer to the examples directory.

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#123-414)[§](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#impl-ConvexClient)

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#134-136)

Constructs a new client for communicating with `deployment_url`.

`let client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;`

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#197-215)

Subscribe to the results of query `name` called with `args`.

Returns a [`QuerySubscription`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.QuerySubscription.html "struct convex::QuerySubscription") which implements [`Stream`](https://docs.rs/futures-core/0.3.31/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/futures_core/stream/trait.Stream.html "trait futures_core::stream::Stream")<[`FunctionResult`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/enum.FunctionResult.html "enum convex::FunctionResult")>. A new value appears on the stream each time the query function produces a new result.

The subscription is REDACTEDmatically unsubscribed when it is dropped.

```
let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
let mut sub = client.subscribe("listMessages", maplit::btreemap!{}).await?;
while let Some(result) = sub.next().await {
    println!("{result:?}");
}
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#236-247)

Make a oneshot request to a query `name` with `args`.

Returns a [`FunctionResult`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/enum.FunctionResult.html "enum convex::FunctionResult") representing the result of the query.

This method is syntactic sugar for waiting for a single result on a subscription. It is equivalent to `client.subscribe(name, args).await?.next().unwrap()`

```
let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
let result = client.query("listMessages", maplit::btreemap!{}).await?;
println!("{result:?}");
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#265-280)

Perform a mutation `name` with `args` and return a future containing the return value of the mutation once it completes.

```
let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
let result = client.mutation("sendMessage", maplit::btreemap!{
    "body".into() => "Let it be.".into(),
    "author".into() => "The Beatles".into(),
}).await?;
println!("{result:?}");
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#298-313)

Perform an action `name` with `args` and return a future containing the return value of the action once it completes.

```
let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
let result = client.action("sendGif", maplit::btreemap!{
    "body".into() => "Tatooine Sunrise.".into(),
    "author".into() => "Luke Skywalker".into(),
}).await?;
println!("{result:?}");
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#345-347)

Get a consistent view of the results of multiple queries (query set).

Returns a [`QuerySetSubscription`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.QuerySetSubscription.html "struct convex::QuerySetSubscription") which implements [`Stream`](https://docs.rs/futures-core/0.3.31/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/futures_core/stream/trait.Stream.html "trait futures_core::stream::Stream")<[`QueryResults`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.QueryResults.html "struct convex::QueryResults")>. Each item in the stream contains a consistent view of the results of all the queries in the query set.

Queries can be added to the query set via [`ConvexClient::subscribe`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#method.subscribe "method convex::ConvexClient::subscribe"). Queries can be removed from the query set via dropping the [`QuerySubscription`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.QuerySubscription.html "struct convex::QuerySubscription") token returned by [`ConvexClient::subscribe`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#method.subscribe "method convex::ConvexClient::subscribe").

[`QueryResults`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.QueryResults.html "struct convex::QueryResults") is a copy-on-write mapping from [`SubscriberId`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.SubscriberId.html "struct convex::SubscriberId") to its latest result [`Value`](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/enum.Value.html "enum convex::Value").

```
let mut client = ConvexClient::new("https://cool-music-123.convex.cloud").await?;
let mut watch = client.watch_all();
let sub1 = client.subscribe("listMessages", maplit::btreemap!{
    "channel".into() => 1.into(),
}).await?;
let sub2 = client.subscribe("listMessages", maplit::btreemap!{
    "channel".into() => 1.into(),
}).await?;
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#366-377)

Set auth for use when calling Convex functions.

Set it with a token that you get from your auth provider via their login flow. If `None` is passed as the token, then auth is unset (logging out).

Internally this wraps the static token in a trivial callback and the same token is re-sent on websocket reconnect.

Prefer [`ConvexClient::set_auth_callback``](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/convex/struct.ConvexClient.html#method.set_auth_callback "method convex::ConvexClient::set_auth_callback") - it will allow fetching a fresh token after a websocket reconnect. That’s important because the original token might have expired while the socket was disconnected.

[Source](https://docs.rs/convex/0.10.4/src/convex/client/mod.rs.html#387-391)

Set an auth token fetcher callback for use when calling Convex functions.

The callback is invoked immediately (with `force_refresh=false`) and again on every websocket reconnect (with `force_refresh=true`), allowing dynamic token refresh.

Pass `None` to clear the callback and log out.

